# Frame

Element with a defined width / height ratio into which any content can be placed.

Content will be stretched to fill the Frame area.

Content which overflows the Frame will be clipped off.

## Usage

```html
<div class="l-frame">
	<img src="/img/image.jpg" alt="Test." />
</div>
```

## Default

<SqueezeContainer>
	<div class="l-frame">
		<img src="/img/image.jpg" alt="Test." />
	</div>
</SqueezeContainer>

## Props

| Property name      | Default value |
| ------------------ | ------------- |
| `--frame-ratio-height--component` | `9`           |
| `--frame-ratio-width--component`  | `16`           |

```html
<div class="l-frame"
	style="
		--frame-ratio-height: 9;
		--frame-ratio-width: 16;"
	>
	<img src="/img/image.jpg" alt="Test." />
</div>
```

<PropNumber name="frameRatioHeight" bind:value={frameRatioHeight} min={0} max={16} />
<PropNumber name="frameRatioWidth" bind:value={frameRatioWidth} min={0} max={16} />

<SqueezeContainer>
	<div class="l-frame"
		style="
			--frame-ratio-height: {frameRatioHeight};
			--frame-ratio-width: {frameRatioWidth};"
	>
		<img src="/img/image.jpg" alt="Test." />
	</div>
</SqueezeContainer>

## With a video

<SqueezeContainer>
	<div class="l-frame">
		<video poster="/video/video.jpg" playsinline={true} autoplay={true} loop={true}>
			<source src="/video/video.webm" type="video/webm" />
			<source src="/video/video.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
		</video>
	</div>
</SqueezeContainer>

## With placeholder content

<SqueezeContainer>
	<div class="l-frame">
		<div class="place-holder">
			<p>Image pending</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</SqueezeContainer>